            <ArticleTitle>Coronary MR angiography.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>361-418</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The principles underlying coronary MR angiographic pulse sequences are reviewed, including basic coronary anatomy, motion, and flow physiology. Coronary MR angiographic techniques can be subdivided into breath-hold (single or repeated) and nonbreath-hold techniques. The recent introduction of navigator pulses for real-time respiratory gating or triggering allows nonbreath-hold or repeated breath-hold 3-D coronary MR angiography, and will allow a more widespread use of this technique.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
